Calibration: in /tmp/di6-baseline-pelqse, make css-verify exits 0 and prints "tailwind.css is up to date". cmp of baseline and DI6 regenerated tmp/tailwind.check.css exits 1 at byte 25416. Node rule-set comparison prints "DI6 added rules [ '.outline{outline-style:solid' ]", "DI6 removed rules []", and "Baseline vs committed additions []". Committed CSS itself is byte-identical across snapshots. Thus this is introduced by DI6, not concurrent DI1 or a pre-existing baseline failure. The new page-refresh.js uses style.outline; Tailwind scanning adds this utility to generated output. This finding does not assert that notice focus styling is absent: inline focus styling works. Missing acceptance evidence is a passing composite generated-asset check. No CSS/source repair performed; lead/worker must resolve within their authorized scope.

Lead integration corroboration for (9): lead reports fresh make check in /tmp/budget2-DI6-release.XArdi6 passed vet/staticcheck/govuln before failing css-verify. Checker independently ran cmp on that copy: regenerated tmp/tailwind.check.css versus shipped web/static/css/tailwind.css differs at byte 25416, exit 1; lead regenerated CSS versus checker regenerated CSS compares identical, exit 0. This is the same concrete integration failure.

